# Kernel-authority closure certificate for the localized universal-descriptor batch

This module adds an independent `assert_kernel_only` check for every public authored declaration of
the eleven approved source modules of the localized universal-descriptor batch:

* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalRule3NumericBound`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedPreparedReferencePipeline`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedDescriptorObservableTransport`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedExtendedFuelMonotonicity`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedRule3SortedParentTransport`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedEndpointObservableTransport`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalDescriptorEvaluation`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedRule3ExclusionExtensionality`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedSpatialSemanticCompletion`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedMutualObservableCompletion`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalReferencePipeline`

Every public `def`, `abbrev`, `theorem`, `structure` and `inductive` is listed, together with the
one authored structure constructor (`LocalizedUniversalReference.Evaluation.mk`).  Auto-generated
structure projections, auto-generated recursors and derived instances are not separate authored
declarations and are not asserted.  Source `private` helpers are proof-internal and are likewise
not listed.

Two changed core symbols are additionally checked, both reached transitively through
`LocalizedSpatialSemanticCompletion` -> `LocalizedOddShortcutSpatialCompleteness` ->
`LocalizedRule3CumulatedDescriptor` -> `LocalizedRule3CumulatedChain`:

* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.CertifiedLocalizedCIPInput.localizedRule3AxisPhysicalContinuationCursors?_nodup`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.CertifiedLocalizedCIPInput.DeclarativeLocalizedRule3AxisTopology.branched`

There are 265 assertions over the eleven modules (264 public declarations plus the single authored
structure constructor) and 2 additional core-symbol assertions, for 267 distinct
`assert_kernel_only` commands in total.

This file contains only import and `assert_kernel_only` commands.  It defines no proofs, performs
no evaluation, and adds no trust bypass.  Kernel closure is a proof-closure statement about these
components; it is not a claim of whole-chemical completeness.

Prior kernel certificates are historical: their checks (including the earlier 1060-assertion
localized batch reports) are NOT rerun and NOT imported here.  This module neither imports a prior
kernel certificate nor a runtime probe.
-/

